  up          Start your development environment (builds if needed)
  down        Stop your environment
  restart     Restart your environment
  enter       Open a shell inside your environment
  build       Build/rebuild your environment
  clean       Remove all environment data
  status      Check if your environment is running
  stats       Monitor resource usage (CPU, memory, etc.)
  logs        View environment logs
  list        See all your development environments
  run         Run a command in your environment

Setup & Configuration:
  init        Set up a new development environment
  check       Verify your configuration is correct
  volumes     Manage persistent storage
  features    Add tools and languages to your environment

Advanced:
  install-agent    Install AI coding assistants
  ssh              SSH key management
  compose          Multi-container environments
  advanced         Advanced configuration options
  integration      Tool integrations
  hostrequirements Check system requirements
  rebuild          Rebuild with specific options
  
Utility:
  version     Show version information
  completion  Setup command auto-completion
  help        Show this help message

Examples:
  dcutil up                    # Start your environment
  dcutil enter                 # Jump into a shell
  dcutil stats                 # Check resource usage
  dcutil volumes list          # See your storage
